-- title:
--   Classical components at full level q of adelic span vectors
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form for $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$, and let $\Phi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ (the general linear group of degree two over the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$) which is an adelic lift of $g$ in the sense of [`CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOf`](def/CuspForm_AdelicLift.html#L14): $\Phi$ is invariant under left translation by the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, invariant under right translation by the image under [`AdelicDock.finEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L145) of the subgroup [`NumberField.AdelicLevel.finiteLevelOne`](def/NumberField_AdelicLevel.html#L418) attached to the ideal of $\mathcal{O}_\mathbb{Q}$ generated by $q^2M'$, and satisfies $\Phi(h) = (g \mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$ for every adele matrix $h$ whose finite part `glFin` is trivial and whose real component $h_\infty =$ [`LanglandsTunnell.ratArchGL2`](def/LanglandsTunnell_DeltaLift.html#L16) $h$ has positive determinant. Let $y$ be an element of [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$ which (i) lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the translates $x \cdot \Phi$ for $x$ ranging over $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$, and (ii) lies in the fixed submodule of [`FLT.SmoothVectors.gl2CongruenceSubgroup q 1`](def/RepTheory_GL2CongruenceSubgroup.html#L181), the subgroup of those $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ all of whose entries of $x - 1$ and of $x^{-1} - 1$ have $q$-adic norm at most $q^{-1}$; that is, $x \cdot y = y$ for all such $x$. Finally let $u \in \mathbb{Z}_q^\times$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a weight-two cusp form $F$ for the subgroup $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ such that for every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ with trivial finite part and with $h_\infty$ of positive determinant, the function underlying $y$, evaluated at $h$ times the image under [`AdelicDock.padicToAdelic`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L254) at $q$ of the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(u,1) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ (the image of $u$ in $\mathbb{Q}_q^\times$), equals $(F \mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$.
--
--   This is one row of the classical–adelic dictionary at level $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$: a vector of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-span of an adelic lift that is fixed by the principal congruence subgroup of level $q$ at $q$ has, along each translate by $\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$, a classical component which is a weight-two cusp form of full level $q$ away from $M'$. It is used to produce the family of components indexed by $u$ (in [`CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOf.exists_linearMap_components_of_fixedSubmodule_of_range_eq_span`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOf.exists_linearMap_components_of_fixedSubmodule_of_range_eq_span)) and thence in the construction of an injection into the dual Tate module of the Jacobian of the full-level modular curve.
-- source:
